WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.361 --> 00:00:15.922
Perda thought.

2
00:00:15.942 --> 00:00:17.523
"We're in Skellia!"

3
00:00:17.543 --> 00:00:20.265
"That's definitely a gulper," she said.

4
00:00:20.285 --> 00:00:22.787
"And it's coming to eat the wormhole!

5
00:00:23.388 --> 00:00:24.909
Back into the vortex—hurry!"

6
00:00:25.609 --> 00:00:28.852
She, Zann, Yarb, and Zing leaped for the wormhole.

7
00:00:29.508 --> 00:00:34.613
Perda was relieved when they were back in the vortex, even though she felt more exhausted than ever.

8
00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:39.637
"Something strange is happening here," she said as they tumbled along.

9
00:00:40.618 --> 00:00:41.359
"What do you mean?"

10
00:00:41.839 --> 00:00:42.460
Zann asked.

11
00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.723
"I'm not sure yet," Perda said.

12
00:00:45.743 --> 00:00:53.310
"But it seems strange that we came out in two worlds we've visited before—Drac and Skellia—but they looked

13
00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:55.212
very different this time.

14
00:00:55.916 --> 00:01:00.339
The mountains were much taller than those we've seen before in Drac, for instance."

15
00:01:01.339 --> 00:01:03.420
"That's not so strange," Zann said.

16
00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:07.623
"We probably came out in a different part of Drac, where there are taller mountains."

17
00:01:07.643 --> 00:01:10.905
"Maybe," Perda said slowly.

18
00:01:10.925 --> 00:01:14.487
"But how do you explain what just happened?

19
00:01:15.127 --> 00:01:19.690
Gulpers are from Skellia, but there was land in that world we just left.

20
00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:23.252
Skellia is completely covered in water.

21
00:01:24.876 --> 00:01:27.718
That's why Wyssa had to rescue Ello's people."

22
00:01:27.738 --> 00:01:33.562
"Maybe there are gulpers in other worlds besides Skellia," Zann said.

23
00:01:34.342 --> 00:01:35.383
Perda thought about that.

24
00:01:35.403 --> 00:01:37.785
"That's possible," she said.

25
00:01:37.805 --> 00:01:42.128
"A lot of species are introduced from one world to another.

26
00:01:42.908 --> 00:01:46.491
Morb brought several horrible creatures to Magica, remember?

27
00:01:47.251 --> 00:01:50.934
And I read that there were no dragons in Magica originally.

28
00:01:51.754 --> 00:01:57.758
They were brought there during the Old Times, probably from Drac or one of the other worlds where

29
00:01:57.778 --> 00:01:58.378
they're native."

30
00:01:58.398 --> 00:02:00.539
"I didn't know that."

31
00:02:01.199 --> 00:02:02.320
Zann looked impressed.

32
00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:05.801
"You really have been learning a lot about Magica's history!"

33
00:02:05.821 --> 00:02:07.482
"What's Magica?"

34
00:02:07.902 --> 00:02:08.522
Yarb asked.

35
00:02:08.542 --> 00:02:10.964
"It's our home world," Zann said.

36
00:02:10.984 --> 00:02:13.045
"It's filled with magic energy.

37
00:02:13.525 --> 00:02:15.266
That's why we already know how to use magic."

38
00:02:16.646 --> 00:02:20.368
Perda was still trying to figure out why the vortex seemed different.

39
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:25.143
"Nobody really knows exactly how the vortex works," she said.

40
00:02:25.163 --> 00:02:29.206
"Not even Wyssa, or the queen of Rood, or your parents.

41
00:02:30.047 --> 00:02:32.289
Could we be stuck in a different part of it?"

42
00:02:32.309 --> 00:02:33.610
"What do you mean?"

43
00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:34.711
Zann asked.

44
00:02:34.731 --> 00:02:37.333
"Wait! Hold on, there's another wormhole."

45
00:02:38.153 --> 00:02:39.074
He grabbed the edge.

46
00:02:39.694 --> 00:02:44.158
But when they looked through, they saw a frozen tundra with no signs of life.

47
00:02:44.858 --> 00:02:46.680
Zann let go and they tumbled on.

48
00:02:49.844 --> 00:02:56.269
"Maybe the vortex has branches that wander off in different directions, like a river," Perda said.

49
00:02:56.910 --> 00:03:03.014
"Or maybe it's like the Wormwood tree, where every branch seems to twist and turn unexpectedly.

50
00:03:04.015 --> 00:03:10.740
If a wormhole leads into a different branch from the one we've traveled before, it would explain why

51
00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:13.202
we haven't found a familiar world yet.

52
00:03:13.863 --> 00:03:19.757
The place we thought was Drac could be another world with dragons, and obviously that couldn't have been

53
00:03:19.857 --> 00:03:21.278
Skellia we just visited."

54
00:03:21.298 --> 00:03:24.458
"Maybe your theory is right."

55
00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:26.179
Zann sounded worried.

56
00:03:26.199 --> 00:03:30.600
"But whatever's going on with the vortex, we need to rest soon.

57
00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:32.360
Let's try another wormhole."

58
00:03:33.281 --> 00:03:35.001
He grabbed the next one they passed.

59
00:03:35.521 --> 00:03:41.383
Perda pulled herself out to look, and a strong, unpleasant, but also familiar smell struck her.

60
00:03:43.143 --> 00:03:45.144
"Ew!" Zann wrinkled his nose.

61
00:03:45.708 --> 00:03:46.569
But then he grinned.

62
00:03:46.589 --> 00:03:51.232
"Hey, there's no way this could be anywhere else but good old Niffia!"

63
00:03:52.453 --> 00:03:54.754
Perda felt like laughing with relief.

64
00:03:54.794 --> 00:04:01.439
The people of Niffia had no noses, which was a good thing, since their world smelled absolutely awful.

65
00:04:02.079 --> 00:04:05.061
As she breathed in, the stench was overwhelming.

66
00:04:05.081 --> 00:04:07.703
"Why are we stopping here?"

67
00:04:08.103 --> 00:04:08.763
Yarb asked.

68
00:04:08.784 --> 00:04:10.425
"It stinks!"

69
00:04:11.345 --> 00:04:13.487
"Yes, it does," Perda told him.

70
00:04:13.507 --> 00:04:15.168
"But we know this world.

71
00:04:15.592 --> 00:04:17.714
Its residents are kind and welcoming."

72
00:04:18.895 --> 00:04:21.537
She and Zann pulled themselves out through the wormhole.

73
00:04:22.118 --> 00:04:24.940
As soon as they unshackled, Yarb grabbed his nose.

74
00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:27.462
"Yuck," he said.

75
00:04:27.482 --> 00:04:29.063
"When can we leave?"

76
00:04:29.764 --> 00:04:34.588
Perda looked around, expecting to see a delegation of friendly Niffians coming to greet them.

77
00:04:35.509 --> 00:04:38.511
That was what had happened on their previous visits to Niffia.

78
00:04:39.452 --> 00:04:40.933
But there was no sign of anyone.

79
00:04:40.953 --> 00:04:43.936
"Let's start walking," Zann suggested.

80
00:04:44.492 --> 00:04:45.953
"They might not have noticed we're here yet.

81
00:04:46.554 --> 00:04:47.735
Maybe we can find a town."

82
00:04:48.616 --> 00:04:50.917
They set off, ignoring Yarb's complaints.

83
00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:56.022
But after walking for several minutes, they hadn't found any signs of civilization.

84
00:04:56.042 --> 00:05:00.425
"Maybe your branch idea is right," Zann said.

85
00:05:00.445 --> 00:05:04.969
"But maybe this branch is letting us out in completely different parts of the worlds than usual.

86
00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:10.073
We could be as far from the Niffian towns we know as the Far Frontier is from Swamp

87
00:05:10.114 --> 00:05:11.295
Bottom back in Magica."

88
00:05:13.344 --> 00:05:15.125
"Maybe." Perda was feeling uneasy again.

89
00:05:15.805 --> 00:05:20.666
On previous visits Niffia had been dotted with pretty villages and well-tended gardens.

90
00:05:21.326 --> 00:05:24.287
All she could see now were wild forests and meadows.

91
00:05:25.067 --> 00:05:27.668
Zing, who was flying overhead, let out a chirp.

92
00:05:27.688 --> 00:05:30.689
"Look!" Zann pointed.

93
00:05:30.709 --> 00:05:32.769
"Zing just spotted smoke."

94
00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:34.690
Perda laughed with relief.

95
00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.731
"That must be a town, or at least a farm or something."

96
00:05:39.411 --> 00:05:41.672
They hurried toward the thin plume of smoke.

97
00:05:42.344 --> 00:05:44.285
It was coming from a clearing in the forest.

98
00:05:45.165 --> 00:05:47.746
A few rough huts were huddled around a firepit.

99
00:05:48.647 --> 00:05:52.808
Several noseless people looked up in surprise when the visitors stepped into view.

100
00:05:53.389 --> 00:05:56.990
They were dressed in drab rags tied together with crude rope.

101
00:05:58.311 --> 00:05:59.871
"Hello," Perda said.

102
00:06:00.532 --> 00:06:04.353
This didn't look anything like the civilized villages she'd visited before.

103
00:06:05.714 --> 00:06:08.675
But at least these people looked similar to the Niffians she'd met.

104
00:06:08.695 --> 00:06:11.076
"We're from Magica.

105
00:06:11.928 --> 00:06:13.929
We're trying to find our way back home.

106
00:06:14.549 --> 00:06:15.389
Can you help us?"

107
00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:17.350
The Niffians stared at her.

108
00:06:17.991 --> 00:06:20.672
Some of them smiled while others looked confused.

109
00:06:21.632 --> 00:06:22.933
One woman scratched her head.

110
00:06:22.953 --> 00:06:27.214
"Magica? Is that on the far side of the forest?"

111
00:06:28.495 --> 00:06:30.496
Perda traded a worried look with Zann.

112
00:06:30.516 --> 00:06:32.917
"Could you tell us how to reach a town?"

113
00:06:33.317 --> 00:06:34.577
Zann asked the Niffians.

114
00:06:34.597 --> 00:06:36.518
"We need to speak with your leaders."

115
00:06:36.538 --> 00:06:38.499
"I am the leader."

116
00:06:39.219 --> 00:06:40.580
Another woman stepped forward.

117
00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:44.223
She smiled proudly as she glanced around at the huts.
